 r←list GetRecentReleases noOf;ind;ids;dates;descriptions;names
⍝ Returns the HTML for the "Recently published" section: the most recent releases, newest first.
⍝ ⍺ is what `Reg.GetAllPackages` returned with its publishing dates, ⍵ how many to show.
⍝ The list is passed in rather than fetched here because the caller wants the same one for
⍝ the figures it prints, and fetching it means reading the config of every package in the
⍝ Registry - once is quite enough.
⍝ The description costs one more config read per row, which is worth it: "what was published
⍝ and what it does" tells a visitor something, a column of package IDs does not.
⍝ Each entry links to the package page of its major version line rather than to the release
⍝ itself, that being the page with the documentation on it.
 r←''
 :If 0=≢list
     :Return
 :EndIf
 ind←⌽⍋list[;2]                                     ⍝ Dates are strings here, so ⍋ rather than ⍒
 ind←(noOf⌊≢ind)↑ind                                ⍝ ⌊ because ↑ would pad with zeros, and 0 is no index
 ids←list[ind;1]
 dates←10∘↑¨list[ind;2]                             ⍝ The day is enough; the time is noise here
 descriptions←{GetPackageDescription G.RegistryPath,'/',⍵}¨ids
 names←Reg.RemoveVersionNumber¨ids
 r,←⊂'<section class="recent">'
 r,←⊂'<div class="section-head"><h3>Recently published</h3><a href="',Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages">All packages →</a></div>'
 r,←⊂'<ol class="recent-list">'
 r,←{
     (id date description name)←⍵
     href←Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages/versions/',Reg.RemoveMinorAndPatch id
     entry←'<li><span class="recent-date">',date,'</span><div>'
     entry,←'<a class="recent-pkg" href="',href,'">',name,' <span class="recent-version">',((1+≢name)↓id),'</span></a>'
     entry,'<span class="recent-desc">',(EscapeSpecialChars description),'</span></div></li>'
 }¨↓⍉↑ids dates descriptions names
 r,←⊂'</ol>'
 r,←⊂'</section>'
⍝Done
